READING:
 (A) #tight&cov == 0  =>  the EQUALITY locus M=1/n is entirely NON-covering: it is certified by the
     explicit witness tau=1/q (THM-523), never by a margin/averaging argument.
 (B) min M(cov) > 1/n  =>  the covering branch has a STRICT cushion: margin arguments have room.
 (C) cushion vs n^2/Phi6(n): the Phi6 resonance is the proved floor n/Phi6(n); the cushion shrinks
     to 1 as n grows -- that, not any n=14-specific coincidence, is why LRC gets harder.
